  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Recently, Chef found a new formula for computing powers of a sequence:\n\n\nYou are given two sequences A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​ and (l1,r1),(l2,r2),…,(lN,rN)(l_1, r_1), (l_2, r_2), \\ldots, (l_N, r_N)(l1​,r1​),(l2​,r2​),…,(lN​,rN​).\nThe 111-st power of the sequence AAA is A1=AA^1 = AA1=A.\nFor each k&gt;1k \\gt 1k&gt;1, the kkk-th power of the sequence AAA (denoted by AkA^kAk) is a sequence with length NNN such that for each valid iii, the iii-th element of this sequence is (Ak)i=(Ak−1)li⊕(Ak−1)li+1⊕…⊕(Ak−1)ri−1⊕(Ak−1)ri .(A^k)_i = (A^{k-1})_{l_i} \\oplus (A^{k-1})_{l_i+1} \\oplus \\ldots \\oplus (A^{k-1})_{r_i-1} \\oplus (A^{k-1})_{r_i} \\,.(Ak)i​=(Ak−1)li​​⊕(Ak−1)li​+1​⊕…⊕(Ak−1)ri​−1​⊕(Ak−1)ri​​.\nAfter discovering this new formula, Chef tried to find AKA^KAK, but he felt that it is very time consuming. Therefore, Chef wants you to do it. Can you find the KKK-th power of AAA for Chef?",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤31 \\le T \\le 31≤T≤3",
      "1≤N≤5001 \\le N \\le 5001≤N≤500",
      "1≤K≤5⋅1071 \\le K \\le 5 \\cdot 10^71≤K≤5⋅107",
      "1≤Ai≤10181 \\le A_i \\le 10^{18}1≤Ai​≤1018 for each valid iii",
      "1≤li≤ri≤N1 \\le l_i \\le r_i \\le N1≤li​≤ri​≤N for each valid iii",
      "Subtasks**Subtask #1 (50 points):**",
      "T=1T = 1T=1",
      "N≤100N \\le 100N≤100",
      "Sample Input`1",
      "3 2",
      "1 2 3",
      "1 2",
      "2 3",
      "1 3",
      "`Example Ouput`3 1 0",
      "`Explanation**Example case 1:**",
      "(A2)1=A1⊕A2=1⊕2=3(A^2)_1 = A_1 \\oplus A_2 = 1 \\oplus 2 = 3(A2)1​=A1​⊕A2​=1⊕2=3",
      "(A2)2=A2⊕A3=2⊕3=1(A^2)_2 = A_2 \\oplus A_3 = 2 \\oplus 3 = 1(A2)2​=A2​⊕A3​=2⊕3=1",
      "(A2)3=A1⊕A2⊕A3=1⊕2⊕3=0(A^2)_3 = A_1 \\oplus A_2 \\oplus A_3 =1 \\oplus 2 \\oplus 3 = 0(A2)3​=A1​⊕A2​⊕A3​=1⊕2⊕3=0"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "The first line of the input contains a single integer TTT denoting the number of test cases. The description of TTT test cases follows.\nThe first line of each test case contains two space-separated integers NNN and KKK.\nThe second line contains NNN space-separated integers A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​.\nNNN lines follow. For each valid iii, the iii-th of these lines contains two space-separated integers lil_ili​ and rir_iri​.",
    "outputFormat": "For each test case, print a single line containing NNN space-separated integers (AK)1,(AK)2,…,(AK)N(A^K)_1, (A^K)_2, \\ldots, (A^K)_N(AK)1​,(AK)2​,…,(AK)N​.",
